# Code\ is this app's git repository and the ONLY folder that goes on GitHub ("push to github.bat").
# Build\, Website\ and Resources\ are beside it, so they are never in it.

# Never public: keys, passwords, shared secrets. The real values live in *.local.* files (or .env) that the build
# uses when they are there; the repository has a blank *.example.* next to each.
# (Fast Share has none: its certificate, its password and every peer's token are made on each PC at first run and
# live in %APPDATA%\FastShare, never in the source.)
*.local.*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx

# Not ours to publish: third-party / Microsoft binaries and tools the build copies in (each app lists its own
# below; README.md says where to get them), and the owner's own data, saves and test files.
# Fast Share's native WPF DLLs (D3DCompiler_47_cor3.dll ...) come from the .NET SDK at publish time, NuGet
# packages (SharpCompress) are restored by dotnet - neither is ever in this folder, but just in case:
*.dll
*.exe
*.rar
*.zip
# FastShare's own settings and logs, if a copy is ever run from here (normally %APPDATA%\FastShare).
config.json
config.json.bak
log.txt
fastshare-debug.log
*.fsold
*.fspart
*.fspart.json

# Build output and caches
build/
dist/
bin/
obj/
release/
updater-tool/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
